{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.GroundRingCore","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.q_param_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.q_param_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L87-L92","doc":"`q · q⁻¹ = 1`. The relation that makes `q_inv_param` an inverse rather\nthan an unrelated element — without it, the pair says nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.one_ne_zero_R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.one_ne_zero_R_q","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L84-L85","doc":"`1 ≠ 0` in the ground ring, in the form a proof usually wants it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.instNontrivialR_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.instNontrivialR_q","kind":"instance","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L64-L82","doc":"**`R_q` is not the zero ring.**\n\nFree by instance search — `LaurentPolynomial ℤ` is nontrivial — but named\nhere so it can be cited rather than re-derived, and so the fact is\ngreppable.\n\nWhy it is worth a name. A statement proved over an arbitrary `CommRing`\noften needs `[Nontrivial R]` to have content: in the zero ring `1 = 0`, so\n`x ≠ 0` is unsatisfiable, every module is zero, and every short exact\nsequence splits vacuously. The zero ring is the ring-level analogue of the\ntrivial instances the vacuity audit exists to catch, and a theorem that\nholds only there holds for the same reason `PUnit` satisfies a class with a\npropositional field.\n\nDownstream, that hypothesis does **not** need adding to the substrate\nclasses. Anything stated over `R_q` gets it from here, which is why\n`QOU/Mathlib/HeckeExtOne.lean` can carry `[Nontrivial R]` in its general\nform and drop it entirely in `groundRing_not_splits_at_neg_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L56-L62","doc":"The formal inverse `q⁻¹` of the indeterminate.\n\nCarried as its own declaration rather than written `q_param⁻¹`: `R_q` is a\nring, not a field, so it has no `Inv` instance and `q⁻¹` cannot be written\neven though `q` is invertible in it. `q_param_mul_inv` below is the\ndefining relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.q_param","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The indeterminate `q` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GroundRing.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GroundRing.R_q","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GroundRingCore.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The ground ring for QOU formal proofs: `R_q := ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, the Laurent\npolynomials over `ℤ`, with `q` as the indeterminate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}